{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Doctor: mapping-config diagnostics with offline-always / live-drift-degrades portability\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe mapping seam (S1–S8) adds a hand-editable `[mapping]` config surface. Two failure classes\nneed surfacing before a reconcile drifts silently:\n\n- **Internally-invalid config** — already fail-closed via `MappingConfigError` (a `ConfigError`\n  subclass): a non-integer `hierarchy` rank / malformed block fail at LOAD\n  (`mapping_config.load_mapping_config`); an out-of-vocabulary axis value, a capability-absent\n  axis reference, and an unmapped-non-skipped type fail in the `rebar_reconciler.config`\n  resolvers. Doctor should surface these as **error** findings, not leave them for reconcile.\n- **Live drift** — internally valid but disagreeing with live Jira (a mapped status/type/link\n  Jira no longer exposes). Surface when Jira is reachable; degrade cleanly when not.\n\n`rebar doctor` is the existing diagnostic home, so extend it, not a new command. It must stay\nportable: it runs where the optional **`jira-datacenter`** extra is absent and no credentials\nare set. Offline checks always run; the live-drift check degrades to an `unavailable` finding,\nmirroring `rebar metrics`'s `unavailable` (`docs/user-guide.md`).\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a mapping-diagnostics function to `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py`, wired into `scan`/the\ndoctor CLI. Mapping findings go in their **own list** (as doctor does for scan-dirty/lock reports), are rendered and folded into the exit code, and kept **out of** `run_repair`'s\niteration — so `doctor.scan()`'s blocking-edge finding contract (and `run_repair` /\n`repair_finding` / `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py`) is unchanged.\n\n- **Offline checks (always run, stdlib-only, no Jira import):** run the provider-neutral\n  `rebar_reconciler.config` resolvers — `effective_status_map`, `effective_type_map`,\n  `assert_type_decisions_complete`, `effective_link_map` — against the loaded config. These\n  inject the built-in `MappingLayer` (`local_to_jira_status` / `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` / link\n  literal) + `Capability`, import `mapping_config` lazily, and are stdlib-only at import (never\n  `adapters.jira*`). Any `MappingConfigError` (non-integer hierarchy, malformed block,\n  out-of-vocabulary status/type/link value, capability-absent reference, unmapped-non-skipped\n  type) → an **error** finding naming the key (non-zero exit). Additionally report one genuinely\n  *soft* problem that is NOT a load error — an all-empty `projects.<KEY>` block (likely stub),\n  found by inspecting the loaded `MappingConfig` structurally — as a **warning**.\n- **Live-drift check (best-effort, degrades):** run only when the `jira-datacenter` extra is\n  importable — gated through `rebar._optional.capability_installed(\"jira_datacenter\")` — AND\n  credentials resolve. On the available path, reuse S8's read-only probe reader\n  (`mapping_probe.build_probe`, backed by `resolve_jira_datacenter_settings`) and diff the\n  configured vocabulary against observed Jira vocabulary, one finding per divergence on the axes\n  the reader observes: **status, type, link** (a configured value absent from Jira's set).\n  Hierarchy is deliberately **excluded** from the live diff: `build_probe` resolves Data Center,\n  and `mapping_probe._hierarchy` documents `hierarchyLevel` as Cloud-only — on Data Center it is\n  always empty and `hierarchy` is dropped, so a hierarchy divergence is structurally\n  undetectable via this reader (offline hierarchy validity is still covered above). When the\n  extra is absent, OR the resolved PAT is empty (`JIRA_PAT` unset —\n  `resolve_jira_datacenter_settings` is total, returning `pat=\"\"`), OR settings resolution\n  raises `ConfigError` (it fails loud on a malformed `[tool.rebar.reconciler]`), OR the probe\n  transport raises, emit a single `unavailable` finding (\"live mapping-drift check skipped:\n  <reason>\") and return success — never raise. The Jira import and settings/probe construction\n  happen lazily inside the check, behind the guard and wrapped so every degradation cause folds\n  into the one `unavailable` finding.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py` — new mapping-diagnostics function (own findings list); the\n  `capability_installed(\"jira_datacenter\")` guard and lazy Jira import.\n- `docs/user-guide.md` — document the offline error/warning findings and the `unavailable`\n  live-drift convention.\n- Reuses S1's `mapping_config` via the `rebar_reconciler.config` resolvers and S8's\n  `mapping_probe.build_probe`; adds no new config surface.\n- Out of scope: `--repair` auto-fixing mapping config (report-only); Jira as a hard doctor\n  dependency; the live-drift **true path against real Jira** — E2E transport is S8's proven\n  read-only probe reader (covered by S8's tests), so this child proves the diff logic through an\n  injected vocabulary and treats the real-transport path as explicitly not-applicable.\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Unit (offline tier), no Jira import:** temp config with (a) valid mapping → no findings;\n  (b) each error-class problem (non-integer hierarchy, out-of-vocabulary value,\n  unmapped-non-skipped type) → an **error** finding naming the key + non-zero exit; (c) an\n  all-empty `projects.<KEY>` block → a **warning** finding naming the key. Asserts no\n  `adapters.jira` import on this path. Oracle: finding list + exit code.\n- **Unit (portability tier):** force the guard false (monkeypatch `capability_installed` for\n  `\"jira_datacenter\"`) → exactly one `unavailable` finding, success exit, no Jira import. Oracle:\n  the single finding + zero exit.\n- **Unit (degradation causes):** guard true; drive each non-transport cause — empty resolved\n  PAT, and a `ConfigError` from settings resolution — each folds into one `unavailable` finding\n  with the matching reason + success exit. Oracle: the finding + reason + zero exit.\n- **Unit (live-drift tier), injected transport:** inject a fake probe reader whose vocabulary\n  diverges on status, type, and link → one drift finding per divergence naming the axis and\n  absent value. No live Jira. Oracle: the per-axis finding set.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar doctor` on a valid `[mapping]` config with the `jira-datacenter` extra absent\n  succeeds and emits exactly one `unavailable` live-drift finding — portability-tier test (guard\n  forced false via `capability_installed`, no Jira import, zero exit).\n- [ ] Each offline error-class problem (non-integer hierarchy, out-of-vocabulary value,\n  unmapped-non-skipped type) yields an **error** finding naming the key + non-zero exit —\n  offline-tier test running the `rebar_reconciler.config` resolvers and asserting the\n  `MappingConfigError`-derived finding.\n- [ ] An all-empty `projects.<KEY>` stub yields a **warning** finding naming the key (not an\n  error, not a non-zero exit) — offline-tier test.\n- [ ] Each non-transport degradation cause — extra absent, empty resolved PAT (`JIRA_PAT`\n  unset), and a `ConfigError` from settings resolution — folds into a single `unavailable`\n  finding + reason + success exit — portability and degradation-cause tests.\n- [ ] With a fake probe reader injected, each configured-vs-observed divergence on status, type,\n  and link yields a drift finding naming the axis and absent value — live-drift-tier test.\n  (Hierarchy is excluded by design: the reused Data Center probe never observes\n  `hierarchyLevel`.)\n- [ ] The doctor module imports and `rebar doctor` runs with the `jira-datacenter` extra\n  uninstalled — portability-tier test asserting the Jira import is lazy/guarded.\n- [ ] `docs/user-guide.md` documents the new mapping diagnostics.\n\nTest tiers: **unit (offline, jira-absent)**, **unit (portability, guard-forced-false)**, **unit\n(degradation causes)**, **unit (live-drift, injected transport)** — all in-process, no live\nJira, no specific CI provider, satisfying `project.portability`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787389545589722001,"uuid":"d4f9bb7c-5cef-4594-b946-f2d1e66cc080"}